{"skill":{"slug":"google-calendar-api","displayName":"Google Calendar"},"version":{"version":"1.2.6","createdAt":1790937536402,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":51808,"sha256":"45d1b11f9bfb667ba12ecb264c162806bd127c4db507b238d5d9f1d28bbad00a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/calendly/triggers.md","size":10281,"sha256":"ae92dbfb6dd4caf628900b293d1b3c6e7d5e70cf7f6a9397407594daf50d4a48","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/github/triggers.md","size":61142,"sha256":"7424d3be38ec400eb8a4b0a6a94a94eeec40208c0bcee29a61caa5da48eea7f4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/google-mail/triggers.md","size":2648,"sha256":"5cc5065cd7db33dc33715675bbb0ee29ed49657ad9ad4354aebd1a9efdf8d8f3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/hubspot/triggers.md","size":8298,"sha256":"439d56e4d02e119e1de3caf79a0334243ae70c583a3e15847831c396f39c2837","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/linear/triggers.md","size":7270,"sha256":"641f6496f50e09faab921ef4c06f725122b798cb034e9f0dfaf9f838074ab377","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/notion/triggers.md","size":5840,"sha256":"fdaf3840d8213dbd7549426c1166f94cc94b09e022a1611ef2dad6f36db2f969","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/slack/triggers.md","size":6181,"sha256":"b5ee099a215223a7e5186c41a0d13fc1de68e977719304c509df105843d81f38","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/stripe/triggers.md","size":25651,"sha256":"ae091545396a376c7ecfe09e94b46b7bbb44fd8a72ea954bcc1239052b7959f0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/time/triggers.md","size":1140,"sha256":"b8f5a523501f8d03e11e58f6426cd96b54ba0c66c8983b57c0ea31386b309e01","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2236,"sha256":"9b2bf0a309c67b9a56d871aecf8c7561c9610714352a2d1c2bfa28c459ea885c","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1790937961681,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d803c955d32de45c62bf76723ddd1669de10778f017fb54e2a05a57037732ee1","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d803c955d32de45c62bf76723ddd1669de10778f017fb54e2a05a57037732ee1","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1790937715171},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1790937961681},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a disclosed Google Calendar integration that can access and modify calendar data through Maton, with sensitive actions documented and gated by user approval.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access, Google Calendar OAuth, and Maton gateway calls are necessary for the integration. Raw HTTP with MATON_API_KEY is limited to environments without the CLI and includes clear secret-handling guidance.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Installation uses pinned Maton CLI packages through npm or Homebrew and requires Maton OAuth login; this is disclosed and proportionate, though users must trust the Maton CLI and account connection.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill includes broad platform reference sections for functions, triggers, and other event-source catalogs, but repeatedly states they do not widen Google Calendar access and require user direction and explicit approval for writes, automations, destinations, and local --exec use.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The CLI stores tokens in the OS credential store, and optional hosted functions/triggers/destinations can persist and run automatically. The artifact discloses this clearly and requires separate approval, least privilege, DENY_ALL network policy by default, and cleanup.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Google Calendar access via managed OAuth, and the documented capabilities fit that purpose: listing calendars/events, creating/updating/deleting events, checking availability, and optional Maton-hosted automation.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust Maton and want an agent to work with your Google Calendar. Prefer OAuth login over API keys, choose the narrowest Google scopes and connection, confirm every calendar write, and review any function, trigger, or destination carefully because those can keep running or forwarding data until deleted.","findings":null,"agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1790937961681}}}}}